1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:39,984 --> 00:01:42,084
Decentralized Institutes of Health

8
00:01:42,824 --> 00:01:46,304
Your military-industrial complex solved coordination for killing:

9
00:01:47,264 --> 00:01:51,484
weapons manufacturers, generals, politicians, and factory workers all profit

10
00:01:51,484 --> 00:01:53,924
from the same budget, so they all show up.

11
00:01:54,604 --> 00:01:56,404
Disease has no such coalition.

12
00:01:57,164 --> 00:01:59,864
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health builds one.

13
00:02:00,364 --> 00:02:01,404
It does three things:

14
00:02:02,044 --> 00:02:06,684
receive treaty funds, allocate them via patient choice and wishocratic voting,

15
00:02:07,104 --> 00:02:10,144
and pay based on results instead of grant applications.

16
00:02:10,744 --> 00:02:15,024
It's the Supreme Headquarters Allied Expeditionary Force, or SHAEF, for

17
00:02:15,024 --> 00:02:16,204
the war on disease.

18
00:02:16,844 --> 00:02:21,184
Same selfishness as the military-industrial complex, but pointed at biology

19
00:02:21,184 --> 00:02:22,384
instead of each other.

20
00:02:22,964 --> 00:02:26,484
Nobody gets paid for writing essays about why they should be allowed to

21
00:02:26,484 --> 00:02:27,364
try curing things.

22
00:02:27,844 --> 00:02:29,664
They get paid for curing things.

23
00:02:30,064 --> 00:02:35,284
I have been watching your species fight disease for eighty years, and I

24
00:02:35,284 --> 00:02:39,944
want to describe what I see, because I think if you saw it from the outside

25
00:02:40,324 --> 00:02:41,404
you would be embarrassed.

26
00:02:42,224 --> 00:02:44,744
You have eight billion of people humans.

27
00:02:45,404 --> 00:02:46,244
Some of them are sick.

28
00:02:46,604 --> 00:02:49,564
Some of them are scientists who could help the sick ones.

29
00:02:49,864 --> 00:02:54,584
And some of them are sitting in offices writing forty-seven-page documents

30
00:02:54,584 --> 00:02:57,464
explaining why they should be allowed to try.

31
00:02:58,144 --> 00:03:00,784
These documents are called "grant applications."

32
00:03:01,244 --> 00:03:04,664
They take six months to write and forty minutes to reject.

33
00:03:05,264 --> 00:03:09,664
Your scientists spend fifty to sixty-seven percent of their time writing

34
00:03:09,664 --> 00:03:10,164
them.

35
00:03:10,544 --> 00:03:14,624
The other thirty-three to fifty percent is spent doing science, which is

36
00:03:14,624 --> 00:03:18,044
the thing they were hired for, though at this point it's more of a hobby

37
00:03:18,044 --> 00:03:20,284
they squeeze in between grant applications.

38
00:03:21,004 --> 00:03:25,264
I asked one of your scientists what a grant application is and she said

39
00:03:25,524 --> 00:03:29,364
"it's a document where you explain what you'd discover if someone let you."

40
00:03:29,744 --> 00:03:32,864
Which means your scientists already know what they'd find.

41
00:03:32,864 --> 00:03:34,824
So why do they need the money?

42
00:03:35,524 --> 00:03:39,764
I thought about this for a long time and then I realized I'd misunderstood

43
00:03:39,764 --> 00:03:43,944
the question, which is also what happens to most grant applications.

44
00:03:44,604 --> 00:03:45,304
Your N.I.H.

45
00:03:45,304 --> 00:03:48,564
spends forty-seven billion dollars a year.

46
00:03:49,243 --> 00:03:52,364
Billions flow to projects that never produce treatments.

47
00:03:52,984 --> 00:03:55,784
Your system isn't designed to cure disease.

48
00:03:56,264 --> 00:04:01,104
It's designed to produce grant applications, which occasionally, as a side

49
00:04:01,104 --> 00:04:02,504
effect, produce medicine.

50
00:04:03,044 --> 00:04:07,124
This is like designing a restaurant whose primary output is menus.

51
00:04:07,904 --> 00:04:10,364
Sometimes, by accident, food comes out.

52
00:04:10,644 --> 00:04:12,444
Everyone acts surprised when it does.

53
00:04:13,164 --> 00:04:14,524
This is not a conspiracy.

54
00:04:15,064 --> 00:04:18,784
It's just what happens when you pay people for asking instead of finding.

55
00:04:19,444 --> 00:04:24,024
You've built a machine whose primary output is requests for money and whose

56
00:04:24,024 --> 00:04:26,924
secondary output is, reluctantly, science.

57
00:04:26,924 --> 00:04:31,904
On Wishonia, we have a word for systems that produce the opposite of their

58
00:04:31,904 --> 00:04:32,744
stated purpose.

59
00:04:33,304 --> 00:04:34,584
The word is "human."

60
00:04:35,164 --> 00:04:36,524
We also use it as a verb.

61
00:04:36,764 --> 00:04:40,884
As in, "the project was going well until someone humaned it.".

62
00:04:41,784 --> 00:04:45,644
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health is what you'd build if you started

63
00:04:45,644 --> 00:04:47,284
over and actually meant it.

64
00:04:47,704 --> 00:04:48,424
Here's the blueprint.

65
00:04:49,184 --> 00:04:50,784
The Health-Industrial Complex:

66
00:04:51,384 --> 00:04:53,384
Coordinating Your War on Disease.

67
00:04:53,384 --> 00:04:55,644
The Olsonian Problem.

68
00:04:56,464 --> 00:05:01,764
Your economist Mancur Olson identified why public goods are systematically

69
00:05:01,764 --> 00:05:02,944
underproduced:

70
00:05:03,544 --> 00:05:06,024
diffuse benefits and concentrated costs.

71
00:05:06,624 --> 00:05:07,624
In simpler terms:

72
00:05:08,064 --> 00:05:12,664
everyone benefits from a cure for cancer, but nobody benefits enough to

73
00:05:12,664 --> 00:05:16,584
fight for it the way a weapons manufacturer fights for a bomber contract.

74
00:05:17,224 --> 00:05:21,344
It's one of those observations that's obvious once someone says it, and

75
00:05:21,344 --> 00:05:25,344
invisible before, which describes most of your species' problems.

76
00:05:26,044 --> 00:05:29,364
Curing cancer benefits eight billion people a little.

77
00:05:29,744 --> 00:05:34,524
But nobody benefits enough to organize, lobby, and fight for it the way

78
00:05:34,524 --> 00:05:37,244
a defense contractor fights for a bomber contract.

79
00:05:37,624 --> 00:05:39,584
The eight billion don't show up.

80
00:05:40,164 --> 00:05:44,444
This is why your species has spent fifty years "fighting cancer" while your

81
00:05:44,444 --> 00:05:48,464
defense industry got stealth bombers, aircraft carriers, and G.P.S.

82
00:05:49,044 --> 00:05:51,184
The defense industry showed up.

83
00:05:52,044 --> 00:05:55,884
Cancer patients were busy having cancer, which is time-consuming in a way

84
00:05:55,884 --> 00:05:59,484
that's hard to explain to people who haven't tried it, and which I understand

85
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:00,664
is not recommended.

86
00:06:01,364 --> 00:06:05,244
Your military-industrial complex solved this problem for killing.

87
00:06:06,064 --> 00:06:10,704
Weapons manufacturers, generals, politicians, and factory workers all have

88
00:06:10,704 --> 00:06:13,444
concentrated interests in military spending.

89
00:06:13,884 --> 00:06:14,424
They coordinate.

90
00:06:14,984 --> 00:06:15,484
They lobby.

91
00:06:15,804 --> 00:06:16,624
They win budgets.

92
00:06:16,624 --> 00:06:18,164
Result:

93
00:06:18,164 --> 00:06:22,644
the most sophisticated death-delivery infrastructure in human history.

94
00:06:23,304 --> 00:06:23,944
Also result:

95
00:06:24,544 --> 00:06:28,124
the most sophisticated death-delivery infrastructure in human history pointed

96
00:06:28,124 --> 00:06:31,524
at everyone, including the people who paid for it.

97
00:06:32,004 --> 00:06:36,484
I looked up "death-delivery" and it's not a real phrase, but it should be,

98
00:06:36,484 --> 00:06:40,444
because your species has been doing it professionally since before you had

99
00:06:40,444 --> 00:06:44,304
writing, which means you were killing each other before you could spell

100
00:06:44,304 --> 00:06:46,724
"killing," which takes some commitment.

101
00:06:47,864 --> 00:06:49,744
Disease has no such coalition.

102
00:06:50,244 --> 00:06:52,344
Your patients are too sick to lobby.

103
00:06:52,944 --> 00:06:54,704
Your researchers compete for scraps.

104
00:06:55,124 --> 00:06:56,784
Your funders lack coordination.

105
00:06:57,484 --> 00:07:02,204
Your politicians get no credit for cures that arrive after their term ends

106
00:07:02,204 --> 00:07:06,644
(which is all of them, because cures take fifteen years and terms last four,

107
00:07:07,024 --> 00:07:10,924
which is a scheduling problem your species has never solved and never tried

108
00:07:10,924 --> 00:07:11,424
to).

109
00:07:11,964 --> 00:07:14,064
Everyone wants disease eradicated;

110
00:07:14,524 --> 00:07:17,604
no one has a concentrated interest in making it happen.

111
00:07:18,084 --> 00:07:21,784
It's like everyone wanting a clean kitchen but nobody wanting to do the

112
00:07:21,784 --> 00:07:25,924
dishes, except the dishes are cancer and the kitchen is on fire.

113
00:07:26,624 --> 00:07:31,364
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health will solve the Olsonian problem

114
00:07:31,364 --> 00:07:35,364
by creating concentrated interests in disease eradication.

115
00:07:35,364 --> 00:07:40,304
It will build a health-industrial complex that coordinates actors around

116
00:07:40,304 --> 00:07:44,984
eradication the way your military-industrial complex coordinates actors

117
00:07:44,984 --> 00:07:47,704
around making humans stop being alive.

118
00:07:48,544 --> 00:07:50,324
Same structure, opposite purpose.

119
00:07:50,904 --> 00:07:52,964
Same selfishness, better direction.

120
00:07:54,164 --> 00:07:59,684
Supreme Headquarters Allied Expeditionary Force, or S.H.A.E.F., for Your

121
00:07:59,684 --> 00:08:00,784
War on Disease.

122
00:08:00,784 --> 00:08:05,224
In nineteen forty-four, Eisenhower didn't replace the Allied armies.

123
00:08:05,504 --> 00:08:06,744
He coordinated them.

124
00:08:07,044 --> 00:08:11,404
Set the objective, allocated resources, made sure everyone pulled in the

125
00:08:11,404 --> 00:08:12,104
same direction.

126
00:08:12,724 --> 00:08:16,804
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health will be S.H.A.E.F.

127
00:08:16,804 --> 00:08:18,344
for the war on disease.

128
00:08:19,144 --> 00:08:20,984
Pharma companies stay pharma companies.

129
00:08:21,704 --> 00:08:23,204
Universities stay universities.

130
00:08:23,804 --> 00:08:25,784
Patient groups stay patient groups.

131
00:08:26,084 --> 00:08:30,924
But they operate as one force because the coordination layer points them

132
00:08:30,924 --> 00:08:34,824
at the same thing, which is the thing they were all supposedly pointed at

133
00:08:34,824 --> 00:08:38,224
already, except they weren't, because nobody was coordinating.

134
00:08:38,784 --> 00:08:43,444
Your war on disease has been losing for fifty years because it's not actually

135
00:08:43,444 --> 00:08:43,944
a war.

136
00:08:44,344 --> 00:08:48,424
It's a collection of uncoordinated skirmishes where researchers compete

137
00:08:48,424 --> 00:08:53,624
for grants, pharma companies hide failures, and patients can't access trials.

138
00:08:53,624 --> 00:08:58,564
You've been "fighting" cancer the way a cat "fights" a laser pointer:

139
00:08:59,124 --> 00:09:00,944
lots of energy, no coordination,

140
00:09:01,664 --> 00:09:02,244
nothing caught.

141
00:09:03,044 --> 00:09:05,244
Imagine if D-Day had been run this way.

142
00:09:05,604 --> 00:09:08,744
The Americans land at one beach, the British at another.

143
00:09:09,264 --> 00:09:11,224
Neither tells the other what they learned.

144
00:09:11,604 --> 00:09:15,404
Both compete for the same supply ships while the enemy reads their grant

145
00:09:15,404 --> 00:09:16,104
applications.

146
00:09:16,824 --> 00:09:21,464
This is how your species currently runs medical research, and you've been

147
00:09:21,464 --> 00:09:25,484
doing it long enough that it feels normal, which is the most dangerous thing

148
00:09:25,484 --> 00:09:26,064
about it.

149
00:09:26,804 --> 00:09:27,984
The R.O.I.

150
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:29,304
Maximization Protocol.

151
00:09:29,304 --> 00:09:34,684
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health will not be a platform.

152
00:09:35,104 --> 00:09:36,344
It won't be an organization.

153
00:09:36,964 --> 00:09:38,724
It won't even really be a thing.

154
00:09:39,204 --> 00:09:43,284
It will be a coordination protocol, which means it's the rules by which

155
00:09:43,284 --> 00:09:44,924
the things talk to each other.

156
00:09:44,924 --> 00:09:50,564
On Wishonia, we built ours four thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years

157
00:09:50,564 --> 00:09:51,064
ago.

158
00:09:51,524 --> 00:09:52,944
It does one thing:

159
00:09:53,344 --> 00:09:58,464
make every actor's most selfish choice also be the most useful choice.

160
00:09:59,084 --> 00:10:01,724
Every dollar flows to maximum impact.

161
00:10:02,164 --> 00:10:05,124
Every researcher works on the highest-value problem.

162
00:10:05,564 --> 00:10:08,484
Every patient joins the trial that matters most.

163
00:10:09,124 --> 00:10:10,524
Nothing gets wasted.

164
00:10:11,144 --> 00:10:13,564
On your planet, you call this radical.

165
00:10:14,244 --> 00:10:16,304
On mine, we call it "obvious."

166
00:10:17,004 --> 00:10:20,844
It's been running longer than most of your civilizations have existed, though

167
00:10:20,844 --> 00:10:24,244
to be fair that's a low bar given how often yours collapse.

168
00:10:25,084 --> 00:10:27,224
It will do exactly three things:

169
00:10:27,844 --> 00:10:31,344
Receive funds (from the one percent Treaty, donations, etc.).

170
00:10:32,364 --> 00:10:37,204
Allocate research via patient subsidies (a market mechanism where sick people

171
00:10:37,204 --> 00:10:41,604
choose which trials to join and the money follows them) and infrastructure

172
00:10:41,604 --> 00:10:46,084
via Wishocracy (where everyone votes on which buildings to build).

173
00:10:46,724 --> 00:10:51,404
Verify results and pay proportional to impact (the part where you only get

174
00:10:51,404 --> 00:10:55,864
money if something actually worked, which is apparently a novel concept

175
00:10:55,864 --> 00:10:57,224
in your research sector).

176
00:10:57,964 --> 00:11:00,184
Everything operational will be outsourced.

177
00:11:00,764 --> 00:11:01,604
Trial infrastructure?

178
00:11:02,164 --> 00:11:04,904
Existing and new providers will compete for the work.

179
00:11:05,744 --> 00:11:07,464
Task decomposition? A.I.

180
00:11:07,464 --> 00:11:08,024
services.

181
00:11:08,624 --> 00:11:09,324
Talent matching?

182
00:11:09,844 --> 00:11:10,864
Existing marketplaces.

183
00:11:11,364 --> 00:11:15,024
The protocol itself will do almost nothing, on purpose.

184
00:11:15,964 --> 00:11:17,064
Why stay thin?

185
00:11:17,724 --> 00:11:20,404
Because thin protocols are hard to capture.

186
00:11:20,884 --> 00:11:22,224
There will be nothing to bribe.

187
00:11:22,664 --> 00:11:24,664
No operational role to corrupt.

188
00:11:25,064 --> 00:11:25,764
No C.E.O.

189
00:11:25,764 --> 00:11:27,284
to take on a yacht trip.

190
00:11:27,644 --> 00:11:31,104
Just rules that move money toward measured outcomes.

191
00:11:31,104 --> 00:11:35,924
Your species has a habit of corrupting every institution you build.

192
00:11:36,524 --> 00:11:39,004
You corrupt them the way water corrodes pipes:

193
00:11:39,484 --> 00:11:41,704
inevitably, given enough time and contact.

194
00:11:42,304 --> 00:11:46,464
The solution is to make the pipe so small and boring that nobody bothers.

195
00:11:47,124 --> 00:11:49,744
This one is boring enough that nobody bothers.

196
00:11:50,524 --> 00:11:54,964
Pay for Results (A Concept Your Research Sector Has Somehow Avoided).

197
00:11:55,624 --> 00:11:59,124
Every dollar will flow based on results, not promises.

198
00:11:59,124 --> 00:12:03,584
Patients will vote with their enrollment, and researchers will get paid

199
00:12:03,584 --> 00:12:04,784
for attracting them.

200
00:12:05,344 --> 00:12:09,664
Outcomes will determine continued funding, so campaigns that deliver will

201
00:12:09,664 --> 00:12:13,044
get more and failures will get defunded.

202
00:12:13,564 --> 00:12:17,944
Nobody gets paid for writing grant proposals, attending review committees,

203
00:12:18,344 --> 00:12:22,264
or publishing papers about why their research might work someday.

204
00:12:23,024 --> 00:12:25,204
This is how most other industries work.

205
00:12:25,204 --> 00:12:29,704
You pay contractors when they build the house, not when they promise to

206
00:12:29,704 --> 00:12:30,204
build it.

207
00:12:30,684 --> 00:12:35,284
You pay farmers when they grow the food, not when they apply for a farming

208
00:12:35,284 --> 00:12:35,784
license.

209
00:12:36,804 --> 00:12:40,404
Medicine, for reasons nobody can explain, went the other way.

210
00:12:41,444 --> 00:12:42,544
Your Data Commons:

211
00:12:43,184 --> 00:12:44,364
Publish Everything.

212
00:12:45,484 --> 00:12:47,664
Your current system hides failures.

213
00:12:48,604 --> 00:12:50,184
Companies bury negative results.

214
00:12:51,084 --> 00:12:53,084
Researchers don't publish what didn't work.

215
00:12:53,584 --> 00:12:58,644
Your scientists waste billions repeating mistakes someone else already made

216
00:12:58,644 --> 00:13:02,904
because they literally cannot find out those mistakes were already made.

217
00:13:03,384 --> 00:13:07,804
It's like your whole species has amnesia, but only for the embarrassing

218
00:13:07,804 --> 00:13:08,384
parts.

219
00:13:08,844 --> 00:13:14,024
You remember your triumphs in high definition and forget your failures completely.

220
00:13:14,644 --> 00:13:16,284
This is called "being human."

221
00:13:16,764 --> 00:13:19,204
It's also called "why you keep dying.".

222
00:13:19,204 --> 00:13:24,224
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health will require one hundred percent

223
00:13:24,224 --> 00:13:29,844
open publication of all data, positive and negative, as a condition of funding.

224
00:13:30,424 --> 00:13:35,664
Every trial, every result, every dataset will be published. A.I.

225
00:13:35,664 --> 00:13:40,164
models will scan the global data commons, finding patterns humans miss.

226
00:13:41,104 --> 00:13:45,124
Failed experiments will become shared knowledge, not repeated waste.

227
00:13:45,124 --> 00:13:50,244
This is intelligence sharing in the Supreme Headquarters Allied Expeditionary

228
00:13:50,244 --> 00:13:52,504
Force, or S.H.A.E.F.

229
00:13:52,704 --> 00:13:53,204
analogy.

230
00:13:53,664 --> 00:13:58,284
Your Allies won partly because they shared Ultra intercepts across commands.

231
00:13:58,864 --> 00:14:03,464
Your war on disease loses because everyone guards their failures like trade

232
00:14:03,464 --> 00:14:03,964
secrets.

233
00:14:04,524 --> 00:14:07,624
It's a group chat where everyone shares what didn't work.

234
00:14:08,084 --> 00:14:12,584
Except the group is your entire species and the topic is death prevention,

235
00:14:12,884 --> 00:14:17,024
which you'd think would motivate sharing, but doesn't, because your scientists

236
00:14:17,024 --> 00:14:20,864
are more afraid of looking wrong than of people staying dead.

237
00:14:22,344 --> 00:14:22,844
Governance:

238
00:14:23,364 --> 00:14:25,744
Sick People Choose, Everyone Else Votes.

239
00:14:26,644 --> 00:14:30,964
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health will use two allocation mechanisms,

240
00:14:31,244 --> 00:14:35,644
because using one would be too simple and using three would be too complicated,

241
00:14:36,004 --> 00:14:39,924
and your species seems to operate best with exactly two of things.

242
00:14:40,304 --> 00:14:44,544
Two eyes, two hands, two political parties, two allocation mechanisms.

243
00:14:44,944 --> 00:14:46,324
Three confuses you.

244
00:14:46,784 --> 00:14:47,624
One bores you.

245
00:14:47,784 --> 00:14:49,204
Two is the human number.

246
00:14:50,084 --> 00:14:50,724
I don't know why.

247
00:14:50,724 --> 00:14:51,644
Maybe it's the eyes.

248
00:14:52,664 --> 00:14:54,644
Patient subsidies will handle research funding.

249
00:14:55,324 --> 00:14:57,884
Sick people will choose which trials to join.

250
00:14:58,444 --> 00:14:59,904
Money will follow their enrollment.

251
00:15:00,464 --> 00:15:04,284
This means research funding will be allocated by the people who will die

252
00:15:04,284 --> 00:15:08,384
if it doesn't work, which is a better selection mechanism than a committee

253
00:15:08,384 --> 00:15:10,684
of people who will not die either way.

254
00:15:11,424 --> 00:15:15,564
Subsidies will be weighted by disease burden (disability-adjusted life years,

255
00:15:15,824 --> 00:15:17,764
or D.A.L.Y.s per patient),

256
00:15:18,364 --> 00:15:23,304
so severe conditions pay more per enrollee and mild ones pay less, which

257
00:15:23,304 --> 00:15:27,024
means every dollar buys the most healthy life-years possible.

258
00:15:27,504 --> 00:15:30,344
No committee will sit around deciding "cancer vs.

259
00:15:30,344 --> 00:15:31,084
Alzheimer's."

260
00:15:31,284 --> 00:15:35,064
The patients will decide, by showing up, and the price signal will make

261
00:15:35,064 --> 00:15:37,344
sure the money goes where the suffering is.

262
00:15:38,364 --> 00:15:41,684
Wishocracy will handle infrastructure and public goods.

263
00:15:42,224 --> 00:15:45,124
It will aggregate preferences through pairwise comparisons

264
00:15:45,804 --> 00:15:48,184
("electronic health record, or E.H.R.

265
00:15:48,184 --> 00:15:53,144
integration or security audits?"), which is a fancy way of saying it asks

266
00:15:53,144 --> 00:15:58,664
everyone which of two things matters more, over and over, until a ranking

267
00:15:58,664 --> 00:15:59,204
emerges.

268
00:15:59,824 --> 00:16:02,704
Your species already does this when choosing restaurants.

269
00:16:03,124 --> 00:16:05,644
You just hadn't applied it to anything important.

270
00:16:07,264 --> 00:16:09,364
Making Selfishness Cure Disease.

271
00:16:09,923 --> 00:16:14,664
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health won't rely on altruism.

272
00:16:14,664 --> 00:16:16,724
Altruism is lovely but flaky.

273
00:16:17,244 --> 00:16:21,684
It shows up when it feels like it, cancels last minute, and is always "busy

274
00:16:21,684 --> 00:16:22,284
that weekend."

275
00:16:22,884 --> 00:16:27,624
Instead, it will pay everyone to do the most useful thing, because greed

276
00:16:27,624 --> 00:16:29,524
is more dependable than kindness.

277
00:16:29,524 --> 00:16:33,124
Your entire economic system proves this daily.

278
00:16:33,724 --> 00:16:35,544
Nobody ever forgot to be greedy.

279
00:16:36,284 --> 00:16:38,064
Greed doesn't need a reminder app.

280
00:16:38,384 --> 00:16:39,744
It doesn't have a snooze button.

281
00:16:40,164 --> 00:16:44,424
It's the only human trait that works consistently, which is why it's the

282
00:16:44,424 --> 00:16:46,144
only one worth building on.

283
00:16:47,484 --> 00:16:51,684
Your researchers will get per-patient subsidies weighted by disease burden,

284
00:16:51,964 --> 00:16:55,804
so treating severe conditions will pay more than treating mild ones.

285
00:16:55,804 --> 00:17:00,584
Your patients will get their trial costs covered, so joining experimental

286
00:17:00,584 --> 00:17:03,444
treatments costs nothing instead of everything.

287
00:17:04,104 --> 00:17:09,004
Your funders will get quadratic matching and outcome tracking, so high-R.O.I.

288
00:17:09,004 --> 00:17:10,484
donations will be amplified.

289
00:17:11,004 --> 00:17:16,184
Your data providers will get fees tied to data utility, so more useful data

290
00:17:16,184 --> 00:17:17,444
will mean more revenue.

291
00:17:18,004 --> 00:17:23,484
Every single actor's most selfish choice will also be the most useful choice.

292
00:17:23,484 --> 00:17:27,084
Selfishness, properly directed, will cure cancer.

293
00:17:27,744 --> 00:17:31,444
The civilizations I've worked with that figured this out are still around.

294
00:17:31,904 --> 00:17:35,864
The ones that decided selfishness was the problem and tried to build systems

295
00:17:35,864 --> 00:17:38,624
that required everyone to be nice are not.

296
00:17:39,084 --> 00:17:40,564
I don't say this to be mean.

297
00:17:40,904 --> 00:17:45,764
I say it because the archaeological record is very clear, and the archaeological

298
00:17:45,764 --> 00:17:47,604
record does not have feelings.

299
00:17:49,124 --> 00:17:50,864
How Your Researchers Get Paid.

300
00:17:50,864 --> 00:17:53,784
Your traditional system works like this:

301
00:17:54,204 --> 00:17:58,724
write a grant proposal, hope a committee likes it, get paid to try, maybe

302
00:17:58,724 --> 00:18:01,944
produce results, maybe not, get paid either way.

303
00:18:02,384 --> 00:18:06,264
It's one of the few professions on your planet where not doing the thing

304
00:18:06,264 --> 00:18:08,304
you're paid for has no consequences.

305
00:18:09,344 --> 00:18:13,524
(Actually, I've since learned this describes most of your government agencies,

306
00:18:13,984 --> 00:18:18,504
except those tend to get paid more for actively doing the opposite of their

307
00:18:18,504 --> 00:18:20,844
stated purpose, which is at least ambitious.).

308
00:18:21,844 --> 00:18:22,724
The new system:

309
00:18:22,724 --> 00:18:27,784
per-patient subsidies weighted by disease burden, with one equation that

310
00:18:27,784 --> 00:18:30,684
replaces your entire grant committee apparatus:

311
00:18:31,224 --> 00:18:31,724
Where

312
00:18:32,244 --> 00:18:38,904
is the subsidy per patient enrolled in a trial for condition , is the disability-adjusted

313
00:18:38,904 --> 00:18:44,063
life years, or D.A.L.Y.s per patient for that condition (from your W.H.O.'s

314
00:18:44,063 --> 00:18:48,444
Global Burden of Disease data, which already exists and nobody was using

315
00:18:48,444 --> 00:18:52,124
for this), and is the value per D.A.L.Y.

316
00:18:52,124 --> 00:18:55,784
(a single constant, tuned to exhaust the annual budget).

317
00:18:56,164 --> 00:18:56,664
That's it.

318
00:18:56,944 --> 00:18:58,803
That's the whole allocation mechanism.

319
00:18:59,464 --> 00:19:03,124
The more patients who join your trial and the more severe the condition,

320
00:19:03,424 --> 00:19:04,843
the more funding you'll get.

321
00:19:05,724 --> 00:19:07,284
Patients vote with their enrollment.

322
00:19:07,823 --> 00:19:12,664
The price signal ensures every dollar buys the most healthy life-years possible.

323
00:19:12,664 --> 00:19:14,864
Cost is handled automatically:

324
00:19:15,384 --> 00:19:20,224
if the subsidy exceeds trial cost per patient, the trial is profitable and

325
00:19:20,224 --> 00:19:21,504
researchers will run it.

326
00:19:21,924 --> 00:19:26,444
If trial cost exceeds the subsidy, nobody runs it, which is correct, because

327
00:19:26,444 --> 00:19:29,504
it means the health value doesn't justify the expense.

328
00:19:30,724 --> 00:19:34,624
Researchers who find cheaper ways to run trials pocket the difference, which

329
00:19:34,624 --> 00:19:39,624
incentivizes efficiency instead of the current system, which incentivizes

330
00:19:39,624 --> 00:19:40,944
asking for more money.

331
00:19:40,944 --> 00:19:45,964
The only thing set centrally is , which is just division:

332
00:19:46,384 --> 00:19:48,564
budget divided by global disease burden.

333
00:19:49,224 --> 00:19:50,844
Everything else is decentralized.

334
00:19:51,824 --> 00:19:56,264
Your entire species has been running grant committees for decades when you

335
00:19:56,264 --> 00:19:58,064
could have been running one equation.

336
00:19:58,644 --> 00:20:01,784
On Wishonia, this discovery took us about forty minutes.

337
00:20:02,204 --> 00:20:07,284
Your species has been at it for seventy years, which is not forty minutes. I've checked.

338
00:20:07,284 --> 00:20:09,844
Results-based continuation:

339
00:20:09,844 --> 00:20:14,724
deliver results and get more funding, or don't deliver and get defunded,

340
00:20:14,724 --> 00:20:20,184
which is how every other job on your planet works except, somehow, research.

341
00:20:20,184 --> 00:20:23,524
Pay your scientists like you pay your plumbers:

342
00:20:23,524 --> 00:20:28,424
for fixing the problem, not for explaining why the problem is hard.

343
00:20:28,424 --> 00:20:31,184
How It Works For Your Patients.

344
00:20:31,184 --> 00:20:36,404
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health won't replace your healthcare system.

345
00:20:36,724 --> 00:20:40,324
It will add an experimental treatment insurance layer on top.

346
00:20:40,944 --> 00:20:43,244
Your species already understands insurance.

347
00:20:43,784 --> 00:20:46,544
I've been trying to understand insurance for forty years.

348
00:20:47,064 --> 00:20:51,604
As far as I can tell, it's a system where you pay money every month so that

349
00:20:51,604 --> 00:20:55,724
when something bad happens, a different person can explain to you, using

350
00:20:55,724 --> 00:21:00,864
very long words, why the bad thing that happened isn't the kind of bad thing

351
00:21:00,864 --> 00:21:01,404
they meant.

352
00:21:01,924 --> 00:21:06,064
It's like a promise, but with lawyers, which on your planet means it's the

353
00:21:06,064 --> 00:21:07,284
opposite of a promise.

354
00:21:07,784 --> 00:21:09,884
This is similar, except it works.

355
00:21:10,724 --> 00:21:12,204
Sarah has Type Two Diabetes.

356
00:21:12,804 --> 00:21:13,844
Metformin isn't working.

357
00:21:14,344 --> 00:21:18,304
Under the old system, she has no other options covered and pays hundreds

358
00:21:18,304 --> 00:21:22,384
per month for a branded drug that's performing about as well as the drug

359
00:21:22,384 --> 00:21:26,084
that isn't working, which is a choice between two kinds of not working,

360
00:21:26,324 --> 00:21:28,344
which her species calls "options."

361
00:21:29,164 --> 00:21:33,284
With your Decentralized Institutes of Health, her doctor checks the trial

362
00:21:33,284 --> 00:21:34,724
network during a regular visit.

363
00:21:35,064 --> 00:21:36,184
Sees relevant trials.

364
00:21:36,604 --> 00:21:38,444
Recommends one based on Sarah's profile.

365
00:21:39,004 --> 00:21:40,424
Sarah enrolls with one click.

366
00:21:40,744 --> 00:21:42,924
The trial coverage pool covers all costs.

367
00:21:43,424 --> 00:21:44,824
Sarah pays a small copay.

368
00:21:45,264 --> 00:21:47,644
Gets an experimental drug that might work better.

369
00:21:47,924 --> 00:21:49,464
Reports blood sugar via app.

370
00:21:49,904 --> 00:21:51,484
Her data helps the next patient.

371
00:21:52,184 --> 00:21:53,624
Total time added to doctor visit:

372
00:21:54,024 --> 00:21:54,544
three minutes.

373
00:21:55,024 --> 00:21:56,564
Total time spent not dying:

374
00:21:57,144 --> 00:21:58,644
potentially the rest of her life.

375
00:21:59,124 --> 00:22:01,324
The ratio between these numbers seems favorable.

376
00:22:01,324 --> 00:22:05,484
Your doctors will cooperate because they get more treatment options for

377
00:22:05,484 --> 00:22:09,944
desperate patients, no liability (covered by trial insurance), and minimal

378
00:22:09,944 --> 00:22:11,024
workflow changes.

379
00:22:11,484 --> 00:22:15,204
Your patients will use it because they get affordable access to experimental

380
00:22:15,204 --> 00:22:19,904
treatments, doctor-recommended, with insurance-like coverage and no financial

381
00:22:19,904 --> 00:22:20,404
risk.

382
00:22:20,844 --> 00:22:24,904
It's like being a guinea pig, except the guinea pig gets paid, gets medicine,

383
00:22:25,284 --> 00:22:29,284
and consented to the arrangement, which distinguishes it from all previous

384
00:22:29,284 --> 00:22:30,284
guinea pig situations.

385
00:22:30,284 --> 00:22:32,264
How the Money Flows.

386
00:22:32,944 --> 00:22:33,504
The Architecture.

387
00:22:34,604 --> 00:22:36,924
The one percent Treaty Fund will hold the treasury.

388
00:22:37,524 --> 00:22:39,384
Money will come in from the one percent Treaty.

389
00:22:39,904 --> 00:22:43,764
It will allocate between infrastructure and public goods via Wishocracy.

390
00:22:44,424 --> 00:22:46,924
It will fund campaigns, not bureaucracies.

391
00:22:47,424 --> 00:22:51,964
It will have no C.E.O., no board, and no one to corrupt, (which will make

392
00:22:51,964 --> 00:22:55,644
it the first financial institution in your history with that property).

393
00:22:55,644 --> 00:23:00,764
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health will be the thin coordination protocol

394
00:23:00,764 --> 00:23:04,744
that receives funding from the one percent Treaty Fund, allocates research

395
00:23:04,744 --> 00:23:08,764
via patient subsidies, verifies results, and pays for outcomes.

396
00:23:09,364 --> 00:23:11,664
It will be a set of rules, not a building.

397
00:23:12,064 --> 00:23:12,864
You won't visit it.

398
00:23:13,044 --> 00:23:13,904
You won't lobby it.

399
00:23:14,084 --> 00:23:15,084
You won't take it to lunch.

400
00:23:15,564 --> 00:23:16,584
This is the point.

401
00:23:17,524 --> 00:23:21,224
Trial infrastructure providers will be funded campaigns that compete to

402
00:23:21,224 --> 00:23:22,544
provide trial infrastructure.

403
00:23:22,544 --> 00:23:25,624
They won't be part of your Decentralized Institutes of Health;

404
00:23:26,004 --> 00:23:30,024
they'll be service providers with no budget authority, the same way a restaurant

405
00:23:30,024 --> 00:23:33,604
kitchen is not part of the building's plumbing even though they both involve

406
00:23:33,604 --> 00:23:34,104
pipes.

407
00:23:34,724 --> 00:23:35,624
The Fund Flow.

408
00:23:36,144 --> 00:23:39,844
Your one percent Treaty redirects twenty-seven point two billion dollars

409
00:23:39,844 --> 00:23:44,544
a year from global military budgets into the one percent Treaty Fund.

410
00:23:45,064 --> 00:23:48,524
Not all of it reaches research, because some of it goes to keeping the machine

411
00:23:48,524 --> 00:23:52,464
running, (which is how all machines work including your current ones, except

412
00:23:52,464 --> 00:23:53,764
this one admits it):

413
00:23:53,944 --> 00:23:58,177
Incentive Alignment Bonds receive ten percent plus ten percent, totaling

414
00:23:58,177 --> 00:24:03,363
two point seven two billion dollars plus two point seven two billion dollars,

415
00:24:03,363 --> 00:24:06,644
to align investors and politicians with outcomes.

416
00:24:07,424 --> 00:24:12,143
The research treasury receives eighty percent, totaling twenty-one point

417
00:24:12,143 --> 00:24:17,149
eight billion dollars, allocated via Wishocracy (approximately ninety-seven

418
00:24:17,149 --> 00:24:21,444
percent to disability-adjusted life years, or D.A.L.Y.-weighted patient

419
00:24:21,444 --> 00:24:25,184
subsidies, and approximately three percent to infrastructure).

420
00:24:26,344 --> 00:24:27,084
What Gets Funded:

421
00:24:28,344 --> 00:24:29,364
Market Failures Only.

422
00:24:30,424 --> 00:24:32,944
Most research allocation will happen automatically.

423
00:24:33,644 --> 00:24:37,704
Patients will choose trials, funding will flow there, and the market will

424
00:24:37,704 --> 00:24:40,084
handle it the way markets handle most things:

425
00:24:40,504 --> 00:24:42,224
imperfectly but vigorously.

426
00:24:42,964 --> 00:24:47,904
The one percent Treaty Fund will step in only for the things markets genuinely

427
00:24:47,904 --> 00:24:49,024
can't do.

428
00:24:50,424 --> 00:24:52,984
Infrastructure includes development and operations,

429
00:24:53,704 --> 00:24:55,644
competing alternative implementations,

430
00:24:56,624 --> 00:24:58,664
data commons storage and processing,

431
00:24:59,404 --> 00:25:01,104
security audits and fraud detection.

432
00:25:02,264 --> 00:25:03,864
These are the pipes and plumbing.

433
00:25:04,864 --> 00:25:06,504
Nobody builds pipes for fun.

434
00:25:07,544 --> 00:25:10,224
Markets don't produce pipes unless someone pays for them.

435
00:25:10,624 --> 00:25:12,364
So the fund pays for them.

436
00:25:12,364 --> 00:25:17,264
True public goods include patient trial participation subsidies,

437
00:25:18,004 --> 00:25:21,304
negative results publishing, and replication studies.

438
00:25:22,304 --> 00:25:26,504
These are the things nobody wants to pay for because the benefit is diffuse

439
00:25:26,504 --> 00:25:28,364
and the payer gets no credit.

440
00:25:29,244 --> 00:25:32,464
Your species has known about this problem since Olson described it, which

441
00:25:32,464 --> 00:25:36,984
was decades ago, and has done nothing about it, which is also decades ago.

442
00:25:37,944 --> 00:25:40,044
This is minimal by design.

443
00:25:40,044 --> 00:25:43,984
Your ecosystem will handle most research funding automatically:

444
00:25:44,964 --> 00:25:47,944
companies will register treatments, patients will join trials,

445
00:25:48,824 --> 00:25:50,864
revenue will flow, research will happen.

446
00:25:51,684 --> 00:25:56,364
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health will only direct the one percent

447
00:25:56,364 --> 00:26:00,884
Treaty Fund to cover what the market genuinely can't, which is less than

448
00:26:00,884 --> 00:26:04,744
you think, because markets are surprisingly competent when you let sick

449
00:26:04,744 --> 00:26:07,544
people choose where to spend money on not being sick.

450
00:26:08,364 --> 00:26:11,864
What Your Decentralized Institutes of Health Outsources

451
00:26:13,044 --> 00:26:13,544
(Everything).

452
00:26:14,424 --> 00:26:18,084
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health will be intentionally minimal.

453
00:26:18,684 --> 00:26:22,904
It will outsource everything operational because the best way to avoid corruption

454
00:26:22,904 --> 00:26:25,184
is to have nothing worth corrupting.

455
00:26:25,584 --> 00:26:28,624
If a provider stops performing, you'll fund a better one.

456
00:26:29,184 --> 00:26:31,064
This is how your species runs restaurants.

457
00:26:31,704 --> 00:26:33,804
Time to try it with medicine.

458
00:26:33,804 --> 00:26:38,704
Trial infrastructure will go to competing providers, because separate concerns

459
00:26:38,704 --> 00:26:40,104
stay uncorrupted.

460
00:26:41,104 --> 00:26:45,324
Crowdfunding will go to existing platforms, because they already exist and

461
00:26:45,324 --> 00:26:48,684
work (your species has already built functional crowdfunding;

462
00:26:49,264 --> 00:26:51,784
no need to reinvent it just because the cause is better).

463
00:26:53,224 --> 00:26:55,524
Talent matching will go to existing marketplaces.

464
00:26:56,564 --> 00:27:00,744
Data storage will go to competing providers, because market competition

465
00:27:00,744 --> 00:27:05,164
works better than monopoly, which you'd think would be obvious by now given

466
00:27:05,164 --> 00:27:09,784
that your entire economic philosophy is based on this observation and yet

467
00:27:09,784 --> 00:27:11,744
your government keeps forgetting it.

468
00:27:12,224 --> 00:27:16,304
Every outsourced function follows the same lifecycle:

469
00:27:16,304 --> 00:27:22,784
propose, vote via Wishocracy, receive funding, deliver, get measured, and

470
00:27:22,784 --> 00:27:25,024
earn continued funding based on results.

471
00:27:25,724 --> 00:27:27,124
This is called "accountability."

472
00:27:27,124 --> 00:27:29,964
Your species invented the word.

473
00:27:30,604 --> 00:27:34,444
I looked it up and it has existed in your language for over four hundred

474
00:27:34,444 --> 00:27:35,244
years.

475
00:27:35,944 --> 00:27:37,664
Time to try the concept.

476
00:27:37,664 --> 00:27:40,284
Anti-Capture Design.

477
00:27:40,284 --> 00:27:43,744
Your current system is trivially captured.

478
00:27:44,344 --> 00:27:48,624
Concentrate billions of dollars in a few committees, and lobbyists will

479
00:27:48,624 --> 00:27:49,204
find them.

480
00:27:49,604 --> 00:27:54,404
This is as predictable as gravity, and your species keeps being surprised

481
00:27:54,404 --> 00:27:58,744
by it, which is surprising, because the surprising thing is that you're

482
00:27:58,744 --> 00:27:59,244
surprised,

483
00:28:00,024 --> 00:28:03,064
which shouldn't be surprising because you've been surprised by it every

484
00:28:03,064 --> 00:28:07,844
time, which means being surprised is actually the normal thing, which means

485
00:28:07,844 --> 00:28:09,644
it's not surprising, which means...

486
00:28:09,644 --> 00:28:11,624
I've lost track.

487
00:28:12,064 --> 00:28:15,084
The point is lobbyists find money.

488
00:28:15,524 --> 00:28:20,344
They find it the way a dog finds a vacuum cleaner, except the dog runs away

489
00:28:20,644 --> 00:28:22,604
and the lobbyist runs toward it.

490
00:28:22,604 --> 00:28:28,544
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health will make capture economically irrational

491
00:28:28,544 --> 00:28:31,264
by removing everything worth capturing.

492
00:28:31,784 --> 00:28:34,604
There will be no C.E.O., so there will be nothing to bribe.

493
00:28:35,264 --> 00:28:39,704
Governance rules will be encoded in transparent, auditable systems, and

494
00:28:39,704 --> 00:28:41,384
you can't bribe an algorithm

495
00:28:42,124 --> 00:28:43,924
(several of your corporations have tried;

496
00:28:44,344 --> 00:28:45,784
the algorithm didn't notice).

497
00:28:46,504 --> 00:28:50,764
Every dollar will be tracked on a public ledger, so corruption will be visible

498
00:28:50,764 --> 00:28:53,064
to everyone with an internet connection.

499
00:28:53,824 --> 00:28:58,464
Anyone will be able to build a competing alternative, so capturing one will

500
00:28:58,464 --> 00:29:00,244
just trigger the creation of another.

501
00:29:01,484 --> 00:29:06,244
